{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And they encamped beyond the Arnon.</b> If it had been written 'in the region of Arnon,' it would imply that they encamped in whatever place they wished throughout the entire region. Now that it is written <b>me-ever Arnon</b>, it informs you that their encampment was only in part of the region — in the portion extending from the border of the Amorite, as Rashi explained." "<b>Beyond the Arnon.</b> And on which side? On that side <b>which is in the wilderness that comes from the border of the Amorite</b> — that is, on the south side of the Arnon wadi, and this is what is called in the chapter of Mase'ot 'Almon-Deblataim,' for it goes out from the territory of Sihon the Amorite and enters the territory of Moab, for the Arnon wadi separates between the two." "<b>For the Arnon is the border of Moab, between Moab and between the Amorite.</b> At first the land of Moab extended westward as far as the Jordan and northward as far as Mount Nebo, for there the border of Sihon began. Through war Sihon took from the side of his land all the land of Moab as far as the Arnon wadi. Concerning him it is said: 'he fought against the first king of Moab and took all his land from his hand as far as the Arnon' — that is, <b>for the Arnon is the border of Moab, between Moab and between the Amorite.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:04.298955785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}